# Cloudflare Pages redirect rules.
#
# These match on PATH only. A rule written against a full URL to send
# www.boost-tourism.co to the bare domain does not fire — tested with www bound
# to the project and serving: it returned 200 and the site, not a 301. Sending
# www to the apex has to be done as a zone-level Redirect Rule in the Cloudflare
# dashboard, where the hostname is actually available to match on.
#
# Until that rule exists, the two hostnames serve identical pages. The canonical
# tag on every page points at the apex, so search engines still consolidate
# there, but a 301 is the thing that actually settles it.

# The pages moved to directory URLs. Pages used to normalise these on its own,
# but adding 404.html changed that — /packages.html now hits the 404 page — so
# the old flat paths are mapped explicitly.
/index.html     /            301
/packages.html  /packages/   301
/plans.html     /plans/      301
